# glm-router settings (copy to ~/glm-router/glm-router.env and edit; every value here is a placeholder).
# The router binary: vllm-router 0.1.17 built from source (tag commit 3451e66, unpatched), see build-router.sh. The
# pip wheel's launcher cannot take --api-key-validation-urls, so it has no inbound auth at all: test use only.
ROUTER_BIN=$HOME/glm-router/bin/vllm-router
# Where it listens. 127.0.0.1 for tests; production needs the address the ngrok-operator pods reach (as serve's
# :8000 today) and then BIND_APPROVED=1 (the user's decision) and inbound auth (VALIDATE=1, below).
BIND=127.0.0.1
BIND_APPROVED=0
PORT=8600
METRICS_PORT=8601
# The workers: one serve per Galaxy, one URL per line in WORKERS_FILE (the start list; add/remove/drain keep it in
# step with the running router). Example lines: http://<galaxy-1-address>:8000
WORKERS_FILE=$HOME/glm-router/workers
# Inbound auth: each request's bearer key is checked once (then cached) by a GET of the workers' /v1/models, which
# serve answers 200 only with its API key; the router sends no key of its own, so the client's key goes on to the
# serve, which checks it again. Every route, the admin API and /health then need the key.
VALIDATE=1
# Optional: the URLs that validate keys (space-separated); default the start list's /v1/models. List every Galaxy's
# serve here when the router may start with one worker (a rolling swap).
#VALIDATION_URLS="http://127.0.0.1:8000/v1/models http://<galaxy-2-address>:8000/v1/models"
# cache_aware as recommended by our routing study: threshold 0.3, abs = slots per worker, rel 2.
SLOTS_PER_WORKER=8
CACHE_THRESHOLD=0.3
BALANCE_REL=2
# Router retries of a 429 (5 attempts, 50 ms x 1.5 by default: a request still 429 after them waited ~5.4 s).
RETRIES=5
LOGDIR=$HOME/glm-router/logs
# The serve API key, for check/drain (read from this file, never printed).
KEY_FILE=$HOME/glm-prod/api-key
# check: alert command (as glm-alert.sh) on a failure, and the share of cache_aware decisions without token ids
# (render failures: the router then routes least-loaded) that counts as a failure.
ALERT_CMD=
MISSING_TOKENS_MAX=0.05
# The patched router (router-media-placeholders.patch in this directory on 0.1.17): route chats with images by a
# placeholder key per image (VLLM_ROUTER_MEDIA_PLACEHOLDERS=1) and break least-loaded ties at random
# (VLLM_ROUTER_RANDOM_TIES=1). Leave unset with the stock binary.
#VLLM_ROUTER_MEDIA_PLACEHOLDERS=1
#VLLM_ROUTER_RANDOM_TIES=1
